From 75eb8cfdb20b77d63e4ef20628dcc573f552f26d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 07:20:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 27/63] kernel/arm: exceptions, signals, syscalls and debugging

- call the exception, interrupt and syscall handlers with an 8 byte
  aligned stack, and save the VFP registers around them
- write all of the SPSR when restoring it; keep r1 and a sane CPSR when
  returning from a signal handler; reset the kernel stack on the way back
  to userland
- fix the syscall arguments and the signal handling on return to
  userland; return the upper half of 64 bit syscall results in r1
- SIGILL for undefined instructions and SIGBUS for unaligned accesses in
  userland, instead of a panic
- an access flag fault on an unmapped page is a page fault; retry
  spurious faults
- fix user TLB invalidation and make the ARMv7 atomics lock-free
- give debuggers the userland registers of a thread; libdebug reads the
  instruction pointer and stack frames

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
